"```python\nfrom django.db import transaction, models\nfrom django.db.models import F\n\nclass Quota(models.Model):\n    obj = models.OneToOneField(AnotherModel)\n    count = models.PositiveIntegerField()\n\n    @transaction.atomic\n    def decrement_count(self):\n        self.count = F('count') - 1\n        self.save()\n```\n\nThis approach uses Django's built-in `transaction.atomic` decorator to ensure that the decrement operation is atomic and thread-safe. The `select_for_update` method is used to acquire a lock on the row, preventing other threads from modifying it until the transaction is committed. This ensures that the decrement operation is performed serially, preventing deadlocks and ensuring atomicity."
