"```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\nfrom werkzeug.utils import secure_filename\nimport os\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n# define a folder to store images\napp.config['UPLOAD_FOLDER'] = 'static/images'\n\ndef insertEvent():\n    # get image from form\n    image = request.files['image']\n    \n    # get other form data\n    eventName = request.form['eventName']\n    price = request.form['price']\n    location = request.form['location']\n    desc = request.form['desc']\n\n    # save image to folder\n    filename = secure_filename(image.filename)\n    image.save(os.path.join(app.config['UPLOAD_FOLDER'], filename))\n\n    # insert data into database\n    # your database code here\n\ndef insertCustomFields():\n    # get form data\n    forms = request.form\n    customInputName = forms.getlist('customInputName[]')\n    inputType = forms.getlist('inputType[]')\n    checkboxes = request.form.getlist('validation[]')\n    checkedValues = [checkbox.value for checkbox in checkboxes]\n\n    # insert data into database\n    # your database code here\n\n# create route for insertEvent function\n@app.route('/inputForm', methods=['POST'])\ndef insertForm():\n    insertEvent()\n    return jsonify({'message': 'Event inserted successfully'})\n\n# create route for insertCustomFields function\n@app.route('/inputForm', methods=['POST'])\ndef insertCustomFieldsForm():\n    insertCustomFields()\n    return jsonify({'message': 'Custom fields inserted successfully'})\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```\n\nThis code creates two routes, one for inserting a single event and one for inserting multiple custom fields. The `insertEvent` function gets the image and other form data from the request, saves the image to a folder, and inserts the data into the database. The `insertCustomFields` function gets the form data, inserts it into the database, and returns a success message. The routes use the Flask framework to handle the requests and responses."
