pending on the BLAS library used and the platform on which the code is running.\n\nIn the provided code, the use of `np.transpose(matrix)` to create a pre-transposed matrix and then multiplying it by itself results in faster execution times compared to multiplying a non-transposed matrix by itself. This is because the BLAS library is able to optimize the matrix multiplication operation by eliminating the need for an additional transpose operation."
