"```python\nimport re\nfrom functools import wraps\n\ndef kebab_case_decorator(func):\n    @wraps(func)\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        route = func.__name__.lower().replace(' ', '-')\n        return func(*args, **kwargs)\n    return wrapper\n\nclass RouteConfig:\n    @staticmethod\n    def configure_routes(app):\n        for name, handler in vars(app).items():\n            if hasattr(handler, '__call__'):\n                handler = kebab_case_decorator(handler)\n                setattr(app, name, handler)\n\n# Usage\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass PackageGroupsController:\n    @RouteConfig.configure_routes(app)\n    def get(self):\n        pass\n\nclass AnotherController:\n    @RouteConfig.configure_routes(app)\n    def get(self):\n        pass\n```\n\nThis code defines a decorator `kebab_case_decorator` that converts the name of a controller to kebab-case format. It then defines a class `RouteConfig` with a static method `configure_routes` that applies this decorator to all controller methods in the application.\n\nTo use this code, create an instance of the `FastAPI` class and apply the `configure_routes` method to it. Then, define your controllers as usual, and the `configure_routes` method will automatically apply the `kebab_case_decorator` to their methods."
"404\n\n# HTTP Status Code Explanation\n\nThe HTTP status code 404 Not Found is used to indicate that the requested resource could not be found. \n\nIn your case, the client is expecting the following:\n\n1. If the user resource with ID 1 is not found, return 404.\n2. If the latest user resource does not exist, return 404.\n\nThis is because the client is looking for a specific resource (user with ID 1 or latest user) and if it's not found, it should return 404 to indicate that the resource was not found.\n\nHowever, returning 200 with an empty result for the latest user resource may not be the best practice as it may confuse the client into thinking that the resource was found but with no data.\n\nIt's more understandable for the client to receive a 404 status code in both cases, as it clearly indicates that the requested resource was not found."
