"import subprocess\nimport os\nimport tensorflow as tf\n\ndef install_cudnn():\n    # Install Cuda Toolkit 11.8.0\n    subprocess.run(['conda', 'install', '-c', 'conda-forge', 'cudatoolkit=11.8.0'])\n\n    # Install cuDNN 8.6.0.163\n    subprocess.run(['pip', 'install', 'nvidia-cudnn-cu11==8.6.0.163'])\n\n    # Set environment variables\n    cudnn_path = subprocess.check_output(['python', '-c', 'import nvidia.cudnn; print(nvidia.cudnn.__file__)']).decode('utf-8').strip()\n    subprocess.run(['export', 'LD_LIBRARY_PATH=', os.path.join(cudnn_path, 'lib'), ':', '$CONDA_PREFIX/lib/:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:'])\n\ninstall_cudnn()\n\n# Verify installation\nprint(tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU'))assistant\n\nThis code will first install the required Cuda Toolkit and cuDNN version using conda and pip respectively. Then it sets the environment variables to include the cuDNN library path. Finally, it verifies the installation by printing the list of physical GPUs available in the system."
