"import re\n\ndef calculate_greediness(pattern):\n    return len(pattern.group(0) or pattern)\n\ndef sort_patterns(patterns):\n    return sorted(patterns, key=calculate_greediness)\n\npatterns = [\n    /foo+ba+r/,\n    /foo/,\n    /foo+bar/,\n    /foobar/,\n    /m[eo]{4,}w/,\n    /boo/,\n    /fooo*/,\n    /meow/\n]\n\nsorted_patterns = sort_patterns(patterns)\nprint(sorted_patterns)assistant\n\nThis code defines a function `calculate_greediness` that calculates the greediness of a regular expression by checking the length of the longest possible match. It then uses the `sorted` function with this key function to sort the patterns.\n\nThe `calculate_greediness` function works by checking if the pattern has a group (i.e., a capturing group) using the `group(0)` method. If the pattern has a group, it returns the length of the group. If the pattern does not have a group, it returns 0.\n\nThe `sort_patterns` function simply calls `sorted` with the `patterns` list and the `calculate_greediness` function as the key function.\n\nThe code then creates a list of patterns, sorts them using `sort_patterns`, and prints the sorted list."
"```python\nimport enum\nimport random\n\nColor = enum.Enum('Color', ['RED', 'GREEN', 'BLUE', \"YELLOW\"])\n\ndef shuffle_with_constraint():\n    colors = {1: 'YELLOW', 2: 'GREEN', 3: 'RED', 4: 'BLUE', 5: 'YELLOW'}\n    balls = [f'Ball {i}' for i in range(1, 21)]\n    result = []\n    \n    while balls:\n        # choose uniformly among colors for the first ball\n        colors_set = set(colors.values())\n        first_ball = random.choice(list(colors_set))\n        \n        # choose a ball of the first color that hasn't been drawn yet\n        ball = [b for b in balls if b.startswith(first_ball)]\n        if not ball:\n            return None\n        result.append(ball.pop(0))\n        \n        # choose uniformly among the remaining colors for the next ball\n        remaining_colors = {c: [b for b in balls if c in b] for c in colors_set}\n        next_ball = random.choice([b for b in remaining_colors[colors[first_ball]]])\n        result.append(next_ball)\n        \n        balls = [b for b in balls if b not in result]\n    \n    return result\n\n# Test the function\nprint(shuffle_with_constraint())\n```"
"def count_pairs(n):\n    a = [0] * n\n    b = [0] * n\n    c = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        a[i] = i\n        b[i] = i\n        c[i] = i\n\n    def merge(left, mid, right):\n        left_len = mid - left + 1\n        right_len = right - mid\n        left_merged = [0] * left_len\n        right_merged = [0] * right_len\n\n        left_index = 0\n        right_index = 0\n        for i in range(left_len + right_len):\n            if left_index == left_len:\n                left_merged[i] = right_merged[right_index]\n                right_index += 1\n            elif right_index == right_len:\n                left_merged[i] = left_merged[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] <= a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] <= b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] <= c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = a[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] <= a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] > b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] <= c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = b[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] <= a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] <= b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] > c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = c[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] > a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] <= b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] <= c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = b[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] > a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] > b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] <= c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = c[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            elif a[left_index] > a[mid + right_index] and b[left_index] <= b[mid + right_index] and c[left_index] > c[mid + right_index]:\n                left_merged[i] = a[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n            else:\n                left_merged[i] = c[left_index]\n                left_index += 1\n\n        for i in range(left_len + right_len):\n            a[left + i] = left_merged[i]\n            b[left + i] = left_merged[i]\n            c[left + i] = left_merged[i]\n\n        return a, b, c\n\n    def merge_sort(left, right):\n        if left < right:\n            mid = (left + right) // 2\n            merge_sort(left, mid)\n            merge_sort(mid + 1, right)\n            a, b, c = merge(left, mid, right)\n\n    merge_sort(0, n - 1)\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if a[i] + 1 == a[i + 1] and b[i] + 1 == b[i + 1] and c[i] + 1 == c[i + 1]:\n            count += 1\n    return count"
