"def longestIncreasingPath(matrix):\n    rows, cols = len(matrix), len(matrix[0])\n    directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\n    dp = [[-1] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    def dfs(r, c):\n        if dp[r][c] != -1:\n            return dp[r][c]\n        max_path = 1\n        for dr, dc in directions:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and matrix[nr][nc] > matrix[r][c]:\n                max_path = max(max_path, 1 + dfs(nr, nc))\n        dp[r][c] = max_path\n        return max_path\n\n    answer = 0\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            answer = max(answer, dfs(r, c))\n\n    return answerassistant\n\nThis code uses a depth-first search (DFS) approach with memoization to find the longest increasing path in the matrix. The DFS function `dfs` explores all possible paths from a given cell and returns the maximum path length. The `directions` list defines the four possible directions to move from a cell. The `dp` matrix stores the maximum path length for each cell, and is updated as the DFS explores the matrix. The `answer` variable keeps track of the maximum path length found so far."
"```cpp\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <random>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdint>\n\nstruct MemoryIterator {\n    using iterator_category = std::forward_iterator_tag;\n    using difference_type = std::ptrdiff_t;\n    using value_type = uint8_t*;\n    using pointer = value_type*;\n    using reference = value_type&;\n\n    MemoryIterator(value_type ptr, size_t element_size)\n        : ptr_(ptr)\n        , element_size_(element_size) {}\n\n    reference operator*() {\n        return ptr_;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator& operator++() {\n        ptr_ += element_size_;\n        return *this;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator& operator--() {\n        ptr_ -= element_size_;\n        return *this;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator operator++(int) {\n        auto tmp = *this;\n        ++(*this);\n        return tmp;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator operator--(int) {\n        auto tmp = *this;\n        --(*this);\n        return tmp;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator& operator+=(size_t n) {\n        ptr_ += n * element_size_;\n        return *this;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator operator+(size_t n) {\n        auto r = *this;\n        r += n;\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator& operator-=(size_t n) {\n        ptr_ -= n * element_size_;\n        return *this;\n    }\n\n    MemoryIterator operator-(size_t n) {\n        auto r = *this;\n        r -= n;\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    friend bool operator==(const MemoryIterator& a, const MemoryIterator& b) {\n        return a.ptr_ == b.ptr_;\n    }\n\n    friend difference_type operator-(const MemoryIterator& a, const MemoryIterator& b) {\n        return a.ptr_ - b.ptr_;\n    }\n\n    friend void swap(MemoryIterator& a, MemoryIterator& b) {\n        std::swap(a.ptr_, b.ptr_);\n        std::swap(a.element_size_, b.element_size_);\n    }\n\nprivate:\n    pointer ptr_;\n    size_t element_size_;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int nrecords = 100, nbytes = 50;\n    std::vector<uint8_t> data(nrecords * nbytes);\n\n    std::uniform_int_distribution<uint8_t> d;\n    std::mt19937_64 rng;\n    std::generate(data.begin(), data.end(), [&]() { return d(rng); });\n\n    int key_index = 20;\n    auto cmp = [](uint8_t* a, uint8_t* b) {\n        int aval = *(int*)(a + key_index), bval = *(int*)(b + key_index);\n        return aval < bval;\n    };\n\n    auto begin = data.data();\n    auto end = data.data() + data.size();\n    std::sort(begin, end, cmp, [](uint8_t* a, uint8_t* b) {\n        return *a < *b;\n    });\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```"
