"from collections import deque\n\ndef maxProfit(k, prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    if k >= n // 2:\n        return sum(max(0, b - a) for a, b in zip(prices, prices[1:]))\n\n    dp = [0] * (2 * k + 1)\n    dq = [0] * (2 * k + 1)\n    queue = deque()\n\n    for price in prices:\n        for i in range(2 * k, -1, -1):\n            if i >= k:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dq[i - k] + price)\n            if i > 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[i - 1] - price)\n        queue.append(dp)\n        dp, dq = dq, dp\n\n    return max(dp)"
