"import firebase_admin\nfrom firebase_admin import auth\n\n# Initialize Firebase Admin SDK\nfirebase_admin.initialize_app()\n\ndef verify_user(phone_number, code):\n    try:\n        user = auth.verify_phone_number(\n            phone_number=phone_number,\n            code=code,\n            app_settings=auth.AppSettings(\n                send_window_time=auth.Sentinel(\n                    time_window=auth.TimeWindow(\n                        start_time=auth.Timestamp.now().add(\n                            auth.Duration(seconds=60)\n                        ),\n                        end_time=auth.Timestamp.now().add(\n                            auth.Duration(seconds=120)\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        )\n        return user\n    except auth.exceptions.SentinelException as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n        return None\n\ndef block_number(phone_number):\n    try:\n        auth.send_sms_verification(\n            phone_number=phone_number,\n            code=auth.Sentinel(\n                time_window=auth.TimeWindow(\n                    start_time=auth.Timestamp.now().add(\n                        auth.Duration(seconds=60)\n                    ),\n                    end_time=auth.Timestamp.now().add(\n                        auth.Duration(seconds=120)\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        )\n    except auth.exceptions.SentinelException as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")assistant\n\nThis code provides two functions, `verify_user` and `block_number`. The `verify_user` function verifies a user's phone number and code, while the `block_number` function sends a verification code to a phone number and blocks it for 120 seconds.\n\nPlease note that this is not a comprehensive solution to stop SMS abuse. You may need to implement additional measures, such as rate limiting and IP blocking, to prevent abuse."
