"```python\nimport subprocess\n\n# Check if the repository is up-to-date\ndef check_repository_status():\n    try:\n        subprocess.check_output(['git', 'status'], cwd='./')\n        return True\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:\n        return False\n\n# Push changes to Azure DevOps\ndef push_changes():\n    try:\n        subprocess.check_output(['git', 'push', 'origin', 'main'], cwd='./')\n        return True\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        return str(e)\n\n# Check if the Git version is up-to-date\ndef check_git_version():\n    try:\n        subprocess.check_output(['git', '--version'], cwd='./')\n        return True\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:\n        return False\n\n# Check the output of the git push command\ndef check_push_output():\n    try:\n        output = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'push', 'origin', 'main'], cwd='./', stderr=subprocess.PIPE)\n        return output.decode('utf-8')\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        return str(e)\n```\n\nYou can use these functions to diagnose the issue. The `check_repository_status` function checks if the repository is up-to-date before pushing changes. The `push_changes` function attempts to push changes to Azure DevOps and returns the output if successful or an error message if not. The `check_git_version` function checks if the Git version is up-to-date before pushing changes. The `check_push_output` function checks the output of the git push command. \n\nIf you want to use these functions in a script, you can do so by calling them and printing their return values.\n\nFor example:\n```python\nif not check_repository_status():\n    print(\"Repository is not up-to-date. Please update before pushing.\")\nelse:\n    push_result = push_changes()\n    if push_result:\n        print(\"Push successful.\")\n    else:\n        print(push_result)\n```\n\nThis script will check if the repository is up-to-date before pushing changes. If it's not up-to-date, it will print a message asking you to update before pushing. If it's up-to-date, it will attempt to push changes and print the result."
