"```python\nfrom threading import Thread\nimport time\n\ndef get_list(sender, e):\n    try:\n        api_data = MyApi.GetDataAsync()\n        main_thread = Thread(target=lambda: MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(lambda: MyObvList.Clear()))\n        main_thread.start()\n        time.sleep(1)\n        main_thread.join()\n        main_thread = Thread(target=lambda: MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(lambda: MyObvList.Clear()))\n        main_thread.start()\n        time.sleep(1)\n        main_thread.join()\n        main_thread = Thread(target=lambda: MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(lambda: MyObvList.Clear()))\n        main_thread.start()\n        time.sleep(1)\n        main_thread.join()\n        if api_data is not None and api_data.count > 0:\n            for data in api_data:\n                my_new_data = MyData()\n                my_new_data.Name = f\"{data.Person.FirstName} {data.Person.MiddleName or ''} {data.Person.LastName} {data.Person.Suffix or ''}\"\n                my_new_data.Number = data.Number\n                my_new_data.Info = data.Info\n                MyObvList.Add(my_new_data)\n    except Exception as ex:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {ex.Message}\")\n\nclass MyData:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.number = None\n        self.name = None\n        self.info = None\n\n    def __init__(self, number, name, info):\n        self.number = number\n        self.name = name\n        self.info = info\n\n    def __getattr__(self, name):\n        if name == 'Number':\n            return self.number\n        elif name == 'Name':\n            return self.name\n        elif name == 'Info':\n            return self.info\n\nclass MyApi:\n    def GetDataAsync(self):\n        # Simulate API call\n        time.sleep(2)\n        return [\n            MyAPIData(\n                Person=MyPerson(\n                    FirstName=\"John\",\n                    MiddleName=\"Doe\",\n                    LastName=\"Smith\",\n                    Suffix=\"Jr\"\n                ),\n                Number=1,\n                Info=\"Some info\"\n            ),\n            MyAPIData(\n                Person=MyPerson(\n                    FirstName=\"Jane\",\n                    MiddleName=\"Doe\",\n                    LastName=\"Smith\",\n                    Suffix=\"Jr\"\n                ),\n                Number=2,\n                Info=\"Some info\"\n            )\n        ]\n\nclass MyPerson:\n    def __init__(self, first_name, middle_name, last_name, suffix):\n        self.FirstName = first_name\n        self.MiddleName = middle_name\n        self.LastName = last_name\n        self.Suffix = suffix\n\nclass MyAPIData:\n    def __init__(self, person, number, info):\n        self.Person = person\n        self.Number = number\n        self.Info = info\n```\n\nIn this code, I have created a new class `MyData` which inherits from `object`. The `Number`, `Name`, and `Info` properties are defined using the `__getattr__` method, which is a special method that allows us to implement a custom getter for a property. This way, we can avoid the `Object reference not set to an instance of an object` error.\n\nThe `MyAPIData` class is also created to represent the data returned from the API.\n\nThe `MyApi` class is created to simulate the API call. It returns a list of `MyAPIData` objects.\n\nThe `get_list` function is created to handle the button click event. It clears the `MyObvList` collection on the main thread and then adds the data to it.\n\nNote: This code assumes that the `MyObvList` collection is an `ObservableCollection<MyData>`. If it's not, you'll need to modify the code accordingly."
"```xml\n<ControlTemplate x:Key=\"CardViewControlTemplate\">\n    <Border Stroke=\"Gray\" StrokeThickness=\"1\" BindingContext=\"{Binding Source={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}\">\n        <Grid RowDefinitions=\"Auto,*\">\n            <Grid Grid.Row=\"0\" BackgroundColor=\"{TemplateBinding HeaderBackgroundColor}\">\n                <ContentPresenter Content=\"{TemplateBinding Header}\" />\n            </Grid>\n\n            <ContentPresenter \n                Grid.Row=\"1\" \n                Margin=\"{StaticResource ContentMargin}\" \n                Content=\"{TemplateBinding Body}\" />\n        </Grid>\n    </Border>\n</ControlTemplate>\n\n<Style TargetType=\"local:CardView\">\n    <Setter Property=\"ControlTemplate\" Value=\"{StaticResource CardViewControlTemplate}\" />\n</Style>\n```\n\nThe issue here is that you're setting the `BindingContext` property of the `Border` element to the `BindingContext` of its parent, which is the `CardView` control. However, the `CardView` control is itself a child of a `Grid` or another `Control`, and you're not setting its `BindingContext` to the binding context of its parent.\n\nTo fix this, you can simply remove the `BindingContext` property from the `Border` element, as the `ContentPresenter` elements will automatically inherit the binding context of their parent."
"```xml\n<ContentPage xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui\" \n             xmlns:x=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml\"\n             x:Class=\"MauiLibTestLib_ConverterIssue.Views.IsEqualConverterPage\"\n             xmlns:mct=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2022/maui/toolkit\"\n             Title=\"IsEqualConverterPage\">\n    <ContentPage.Resources>\n        <x:String x:Key=\"MAUI\">MAUI</x:String>\n        <mct:IsEqualConverter x:Key=\"IsEqualConverter\" />\n    </ContentPage.Resources>\n\n    <!-- \n        The code in VerticalStackLayout was taken from the MAUI community toolkit sample code here:\n        https://github.com/CommunityToolkit/Maui/blob/main/samples/CommunityToolkit.Maui.Sample/Pages/Converters/IsEqualConverterPage.xaml\n    -->\n\n    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing=\"10\">\n        <Label Text=\"The IsEqualConverter is a converter that allows users to convert any value binding to a bool depending on whether or not it is equal to a different value. The initial binding contains the object that will be compared and the ConverterParameter contains the object to compare it to.\" />\n        <Entry Margin=\"0\" Text=\"{Binding InputValue}\" HorizontalOptions=\"FillAndExpand\" />\n        <Label Text=\"Does the entry text equal \\\"MAUI\\\"?\" />\n        <Label FontSize=\"Large\" HorizontalOptions=\"FillAndExpand\" Text=\"Yes, it does!\" TextColor=\"Green\">\n            <Label.Triggers>\n                <DataTrigger TargetType=\"Label\" Binding=\"{Binding InputValue, Converter={StaticResource IsEqualConverter}, ConverterParameter={StaticResource MAUI}}\" Value=\"False\">\n                    <Setter Property=\"Text\" Value=\"No, it doesn't\" />\n                    <Setter Property=\"TextColor\" Value=\"Red\" />\n                </DataTrigger>\n            </Label.Triggers>\n        </Label>\n    </VerticalStackLayout>\n</ContentPage>\n```"
