"```python\ndef compare_card_texts(last_card_text, current_card_text):\n    if last_card_text == current_card_text:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n\n# Initialize variables\nscroll_array = list(range(1, 101))\nstop_scroll = False\n\n# Loop through each item in the scroll array\nfor index, item in enumerate(scroll_array):\n    if stop_scroll:\n        break\n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"card\"]').eq(index).then(lambda element: \n        last_card_text = element.text())\n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"footer\"]').scrollIntoView().should('be.visible')\n    cy.wait(1000)\n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"card\"]').eq(index + 1).then(lambda element: \n        current_card_text = element.text())\n    if compare_card_texts(last_card_text, current_card_text):\n        stop_scroll = True\n```\n\nThe issue with your original code lies in the way you're using `cy.wrap(scrollArray).each()`. This function does not support the syntax you're using. Also, the condition `if (stopScroll != true)` should be outside the callback function.\n\nAdditionally, I've used `lambda` functions to get the text of the elements because `cy.get()` returns a promise. We need to wait for it to resolve before accessing its properties.\n\nIn this code, we loop through each item in the `scroll_array`. Inside the loop, we get the text of the last card, scroll down, get the text of the current card, and compare them. If they're the same, we set `stop_scroll` to `True` and break out of the loop."
