"```python\nfrom kubernetes import client, config\n\n# Load the configuration\nconfig.load_kube_config()\n\n# Create a CoreV1Api object\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n\n# Get the node object\nnode = v1.read_namespaced_node(\"ip-10-0-12-61.ec2.internal\", \"default\")\n\n# Check if the node has a taint\nif node.spec.taints:\n    for taint in node.spec.taints:\n        if taint.key == \"node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable\":\n            print(f\"Node {node.metadata.name} has a taint with key {taint.key} and effect {taint.effect}\")\n            print(f\"Node {node.metadata.name} has a toleration for the taint with key {taint.key} and effect {taint.effect}\")\n            break\nelse:\n    print(f\"Node {node.metadata.name} does not have any taints\")\n\n# Try to create a pod on the node\npod = v1.create_namespaced_pod(\n    namespace=\"default\",\n    pod_spec=client.V1PodSpec(\n        containers=[\n            client.V1Container(\n                name=\"test\",\n                image=\"nginx:latest\",\n                resources=client.V1ResourceRequirements(\n                    requests=client.V1ResourceRequirements(\n                        cpu=\"100m\",\n                        memory=\"128Mi\"\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        ],\n        tolerations=[\n            client.V1Toleration(\n                key=\"node.kubernetes.io/not-ready\",\n                operator=\"Exists\",\n                effect=\"NoExecute\"\n            ),\n            client.V1Toleration(\n                key=\"node.kubernetes.io/unreachable\",\n                operator=\"Exists\",\n                effect=\"NoExecute\"\n            )\n        ]\n    )\n)\n\nprint(pod.metadata.name)\n```\n\nThis script checks if the node has a taint and if it does, it tries to create a pod with a toleration for the taint. If the node does not have a taint, it creates a pod without any tolerations. The pod is created with a CPU request of 100m and a memory request of 128Mi."
