"```python\n# Define the old and new API versions for HorizontalPodAutoscaler\nold_api_version = \"autoscaling/v2beta1\"\nnew_api_version = \"autoscaling/v2\"\n\n# Define the command to upgrade the Helm release\nupgrade_command = f\"helm upgrade --install {old_api_version} --set apiVersion={new_api_version} ...\"\n\n# Define the command to uninstall the Helm release\nuninstall_command = \"helm uninstall ...\"\n\n# Define the command to reinstall the Helm release\nreinstall_command = f\"helm install ... --set apiVersion={new_api_version} ...\"\n```\n\nExplanation:\n\nThe error occurs because the new version of Kubernetes (1.25) has changed the default API version for HorizontalPodAutoscaler to `autoscaling/v2`, which is different from the version specified in the `helm upgrade` command (`autoscaling/v2beta1`). To fix this issue without reinstalling the release, you can update the `apiVersion` setting in the `values.yaml` file of the Helm chart to point to the new API version (`autoscaling/v2`). Then, you can use the `helm upgrade` command with the `--set` flag to apply the changes.\n\nFor example, you can add the following line to the `values.yaml` file:\n```yml\napiVersion: autoscaling/v2\n```\nAfter making this change, you can run the following command to upgrade the Helm release:\n```bash\nhelm upgrade --install ... --set apiVersion=autoscaling/v2 ...\n```\nThis should resolve the error and update the HorizontalPodAutoscaler to use the new API version."
