"```python\nname: CICD\n\n# ...\n\njobs:\n  CI:\n    uses: ...\n  CD:\n    needs: [CI]\n    when: on_success\n    env:\n      GITHUB Disability: true\n```\n\nIn the above code, we are using the `when` directive to run the CD job only when the CI job is successful. This way, the CD job will not run if the CI job fails, effectively disabling it.\n\nWe are also setting an environment variable `GITHUB Disability` to `true` to preserve the version control history.\n\nNote: This approach only disables the CD job temporarily and will not affect its future runs. If you want to permanently disable the CD job, you will need to use the GitHub UI, REST API, or GitHub CLI as mentioned in the GitHub documentation."
